{"name":"Hopscotch","hex":"#afbb42","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hopscotch","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A child's game, in which a player, hopping on one foot, drives a stone from one compartment to another of a figure traced or scotched on the ground."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move by hopping.","To move back and forth between adjacent patterns by or as if by hopping."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hopscotch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hopscotch","blocks":[{"text":"Hopscotch is a playground game popular in many countries around the world. Players toss a small object, sometimes called a piggy or lagger, into numbered triangles or a pattern of rectangles outlined on the ground and then hop or jump through the spaces and retrieve the object. It is a children's game that can be played with several players or alone. Hopscotch is a physical and cognitive workout."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Hopscotch_in_California.jpg/330px-Hopscotch_in_California.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hopscotch","wikidata":"Q27981"},{"title":"Hopscotch (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Hopscotch is a 1980 American comedy spy film directed by Ronald Neame and starring Walter Matthau, Glenda Jackson, Sam Waterston, Ned Beatty and Herbert Lom. The screenplay was written by Bryan Forbes and Brian Garfield, based on Garfield's 1975 novel."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c3/Hopscotchposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hopscotch_(film)","wikidata":"Q53095"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/30/ICKA.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/30/ICKA.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedi